<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via 3-day fixed system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via 3-day fixed system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve injected reserves into the banking system via three-day fixed system repurchase agreements on Monday, a New York Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>The operation was expected. The federal funds rate was at 5-9/16 percent when the Fed entered the open market.</p>
<p>Market sources still said that a permanent injection of reserves via an outright purchase of bills is possible as early as this week.</p>
<p>((-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660))</p>
